# netsurf: flex boxes and inline-blocks built again whole for changes in their own content (patch 438)
# Generated 2026-11-22
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 437)
#
# Three changes declined into the full rebuild:
#  - "nearest box is not a block": the child list of an inline-block
#    <button> (wpnews), and text or innerHTML set on a flex box itself
#    (youtube's <main> / <c-wiz>: no class, attribute or child-list mark);
#  - "a flex or grid box's child list changed in elements with a box"
#    (patch 408 answered only box-less children).
#
# A flex or grid box whose own content changes is built again whole by
# html_rl_flex_whole, through 372's container rebuild (cascaded afresh from
# the DOM, controls handed over, objects and frames carried, the page laid
# out whole). Its children are all rebuilt, so what a structural or
# sibling rule sees among them is cascaded afresh; only its own :empty,
# flipped by the change, reaches outside, and 373's check declines that
# when a + / ~ rule tests :empty. An inline-block, inline-flex or
# inline-grid box sits in its block's line as an inline does: the walk goes
# on up to the block, whose path builds a line that is not plain inline
# content again whole (425/434). Its own class is answered before.
#
